  "notes": "Backend: default/production backend is Blitz. The `fulgur` facade crate is `pub use fulgur_blitz::*` (crates/fulgur/src/lib.rs:8) and the published CLI depends only on it (crates/fulgur-cli/Cargo.toml). Other backend: crates/fulgur-raikiri ('Raikiri backend for Fulgur, under development', crates/fulgur-raikiri/README.md), selectable only through the unpublished crates/fulgur-dev CLI (`--engine blitz|raikiri`, default blitz). Not used here. Adapter: AssetBundle::new + add_css(\"@page { size: Wpx Hpx; margin: Mpx; }\") + add_image_file(...) (crates/fulgur-core/src/asset.rs:76,101,358), then Engine::builder().base_path(<canonical input dir>).assets(bundle).build().render(html) (crates/fulgur-blitz/src/engine.rs:76,1426,1416,1446,123). Stdout isolation and log capture are copied from crates/fulgur-cli/src/main.rs:18-48,69-160, because blitz-html println!s parse errors to stdout. page_rule: @page size/margin from the AssetBundle CSS, <link>/@import CSS and inline <style> are merged in that order (engine.rs:191-219), :first/:left/:right are handled by gcpm/page_settings.rs:202-298, and margin boxes/running elements are rendered. Pagination uses the page-1 content height for all pages (engine.rs:580-590). default_page_size_config partial: EngineBuilder::page_size/margin set Config::overrides (crates/fulgur-core/src/config.rs:310-319), and overrides beat author @page (page_settings.rs:239,289). There is no builder API for a default that @page can override (fulgur-dev does the same, crates/fulgur-dev/src/blitz.rs:18-26). So the adapter injects the default as the first @page rule via AssetBundle CSS (default layer, so later author rules override per property; px is accepted, gcpm/parser.rs:288-298). Caveat: an author `size: auto|landscape|portrait` (no explicit dimensions) resolves against Config::page_size, which stays at the A4 default, not WxH (page_settings.rs:252-263,279-281). local_resources partial: base URL = file:// of the canonical input dir (blitz_adapter.rs:206,309,450). FulgurNetProvider loads <link>/@import/font/image bytes only from file:// paths that canonicalize INSIDE that dir, so ../ and absolute paths outside it are rejected by design (net.rs:1-11,157-167). Painted images come ONLY from the AssetBundle (convert/replaced.rs:186-200, convert/style/background.rs:43-50; lookup by authored src or base-relative resolved CSS URL, asset.rs:305-320,452-466). The adapter therefore walks the input dir (depth 8, 20k entries) and bundles each png/jpg/jpeg/gif/svg whose file name appears in the HTML or in any .css under the dir, keyed by base-relative path (plus a percent-encoded variant). Upstream examples do this per-directory via --image (mise.toml update-examples). system_fonts: Blitz default FontContext with fontique system fonts when no bundled fonts (blitz_adapter.rs:427-430; fontique 0.6 uses yeslogic-fontconfig-sys, Cargo.lock). font_face partial: @font-face url() is fetched by Blitz through the same sandboxed FulgurNetProvider; no upstream test covers url()-loaded @font-face (only bundled fonts, crates/fulgur-wpt/tests/fonts_integration.rs), so it is unverified. geometry partial: Engine::layout (engine.rs:845) returns LayoutOutput.geometry = BTreeMap<node id, PaginationGeometry{fragments: [Fragment{page_index,x,y,width,height}]}> in CSS px (engine.rs:28-30; pagination_layout.rs:73-86,137). x is html-relative and y is content-box-relative. Page-absolute px follows render.rs:104-115,274-284: x = margin_left + frag.x, y = margin_top + frag.y (+ drawables.body_offset_pt.y on page 0 only, drawables.rs:409). LayoutOutput does not surface the resolved page box (engine.rs:41-46), so the adapter re-derives per-page size/margin with gcpm::parser::parse_gcpm + blitz_adapter::parse_html_with_local_resources + extract_gcpm_from_inline_styles + gcpm::page_settings::resolve_page_settings, mirroring engine.rs:183-249. Tag/id/class come from that re-parsed DOM by node id (blitz_adapter.rs:250,1950), cross-checked against drawables block/paragraph ids; disagreeing nodes are dropped and reported in diagnostics. Excluded: @page margin boxes and running elements (engine.rs:32-39), text nodes, inline-block content painted under a transform (drawables.inline_box_subtree_skip). Page count = pagination_layout::implied_page_count (pagination_layout.rs:4775, same as render.rs:65). diagnostics partial: there is no structured warning API. The adapter installs a log::Log that captures every Warn/Error record emitted during render (29 log::warn! sites in fulgur-blitz/fulgur-core, e.g. gcpm/page_settings.rs unknown page-size keyword) as kind '<level>:<target>'. blitz-html parse errors are println!s and go to stderr, not diagnostics. javascript: none (no JS engine in the dependency tree). svg partial: inline <svg> is rendered via usvg/krilla-svg (convert/replaced.rs:26,219-240), and SVG works as CSS background/list-marker (image.rs:27-41, background.rs:52), but <img src=*.svg> is not painted (convert_image accepts raster only, replaced.rs:200 via image.rs:157-167). images partial: PNG/JPEG/GIF only (image.rs:7-11,157-167), no WebP/AVIF, and only via the AssetBundle. Stdout page count via lopdf::Document::load_mem(..).get_pages().len() (pattern from crates/fulgur/tests/render_smoke.rs:1729-1731). Toolchain: workspace edition 2024, rust-version 1.89.0 (Cargo.toml [workspace.package]); no rust-toolchain.toml; mise.toml rust=latest; upstream CI uses dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable. Upstream has no [workspace.dependencies], so the adapter declares fulgur by path and log/serde_json/lopdf/libc by the same version reqs as upstream members (all already in Cargo.lock). apt: libfontconfig1-dev + pkg-config as in upstream release-plz.yml:349-356 (yeslogic-fontconfig-sys build script); fontconfig for runtime discovery."
}
